From 34a53b6a7c6db8f2d75460823037cc4da8400986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bianca Giocas <bgiocas@arista.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:50:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: aspeed: Update AST2700 platform peripherals

Align the local AST2700 common DTS and pinctrl descriptions with the
Aspeed v6.18 tree while retaining the local flattened
interrupt-controller topology. Update the SRAM mappings, pinctrl
register windows, SoC1 clock assignments, UART descriptions, SPI2,
MDIO, JTAG1, and LPC0 UART-routing node.

Add the UART TX/RX and JTAG reset pinctrl states required by the
updated AST2700 peripheral nodes.

Ported from: https://github.com/AspeedTech-BMC/linux/blob/aspeed-master-v6.18/arch/arm64/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-g7.dtsi
Upstreaming in progress: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-aspeed/20250904103401.88287-5-billy_tsai@aspeedtech.com/

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bianca Giocas <bgiocas@arista.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-g7-common.dtsi     | 142 ++++++++++++++----
 .../boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-g7-pinctrl.dtsi    | 114 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 224 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-g7-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-g7-common.dtsi
